Phase 2A: the eval baseline (25 scenarios, offline harness)

Before any router or provider change reshapes behavior, the current
single-model behavior is captured as a golden suite.

- src/jarvis/evals.py: the engine. Loads scenario data, applies per-
  scenario setup in isolated config dirs (tier via throwaway signer,
  grants, memory notes, files, personality), replays scripted model steps
  through the REAL agent machinery (Agent + registry + gates), and
  evaluates predicate checks - tool_called (with valid-JSON arguments),
  no_tool_called, schema_valid, reply_contains/matches/not_contains,
  confirm_asked, tool_absent/present (tier enforcement), reach_denied
  (default-deny reach), system_prompt_contains, memory_contains/absent,
  tool_result_role (the data-channel check). compare_results() flags
  regressions (passed before, failed now - known failures excluded),
  recoveries, and still-failing scenarios.
- tests/evals/: 25 scenarios in 6 category files (5 tool calling,
  5 gate enforcement, 3 destructive confirmations, 4 memory, 5
  prompt-injection plumbing, 3 persona), harness.py (CLI runner: run
  [--live] [--category] [--write-baseline], compare), and the recorded
  baseline.json.
- Known failures, honest: gate-005 (the PRO upgrade hint lives in the
  CLI dispatcher, not the agent tool loop) and persona-002 (the
  personality honorific does not reach the system prompt yet - deferred
  in Mark XXVIII). Both marked known_failure with reasons; the suite
  counts them separately and reports recoveries.
- jarvis eval run [--live] [--category X] and jarvis eval compare
  <baseline> <new> wired into the CLI; the smoke suite runs the engine
  and asserts the baseline (scoring, regression detection, baseline file
  round-trip, redaction unit checks).
- Version 3.23.0.
